# ⚡ Tropsi X Kernel

**Custom Non-GKI Kernel for the OnePlus kona platform**

![Kernel](https://img.shields.io/badge/KERNEL-4.19.325--cip132-blue?style=for-the-badge)
![Root](https://img.shields.io/badge/ROOT-KernelSU-orange?style=for-the-badge)
![Toolchain](https://img.shields.io/badge/TOOLCHAIN-Neutron%20Clang-success?style=for-the-badge)
![Base](https://img.shields.io/badge/BASE-ppajda%20XTD-critical?style=for-the-badge)

</div>

---

> [!WARNING]
> Flashing a custom kernel carries risk of instability, bootloops, or other issues. You flash at your own risk — the maintainer is not responsible for any damage to your device.

## 📱 Supported Devices

| Device | Codename |
|:---|:---|
| OnePlus 8 | instantnoodle |
| OnePlus 8 Pro | instantnoodlep |
| OnePlus 8T | kebab |
| OnePlus 9R | lemonades |

## 🧩 Build Info

| Component | Details |
|:---|:---|
| Kernel | Linux 4.19.325-cip132 |
| Root Solution | KernelSU |
| Toolchain | Neutron Clang 19.0.0 + Neutron LLD |
| Base | ppajda's XTD kernel |
| Branch | `sm8250_t_13.1_op8` |

## ✨ Features

| Feature | Detail |
|:---|:---|
| I/O Scheduler | Zen |
| ZRAM | 4GB, LZ4 compression |
| TCP Congestion Control | Westwood |
| Input Boost | Tuned frequency/duration |

## 🚀 Flashing

1. Grab the latest build from [Releases](https://github.com/TropsPk/Tropsi_X_Kernel/releases)
2. Flash via custom recovery (AnyKernel3 zip), or `fastboot boot` to test first
3. Reboot

